 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Totally normal feeling. The key is low-key confidence. Imagine you' showing up at someone's private bar, rather than being in the spotlight. Try to notice them without getting caught in them. A short breath before speaking helps too. Speaking softly with some pauses helps too. Dress smart casual, so you feel comfortable without standing out. Don' worry about it. Order something simple and straightforward. People at nice restaurants want you to enjoy it, not for it to be a disaster. Not necessarily, though it' nice to see what else is on offer. A simple plate puts food right in front of you, so you and your partner can focus on each other rather than the food.",
